  "actions": "1. Revise and enforce mandatory pre-maintenance checklist to include explicit steps for system isolation, depressurization, and drain valve closure with dual verification. 2. Relocate spill kits to within 10 meters of all hydraulic maintenance work areas. 3. Implement mandatory refresher training on spill prevention and emergency response for all maintenance personnel, with competency assessment. 4. Introduce a pre-work safety huddle for high-risk tasks, documented and signed off by supervisor. 5. Install automated drain valve interlocks that prevent line disconnection unless valve is closed and system is depressurized.",
